WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
SPEAKER: Welcome to this
episode of "Click to Deploy,"

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.500
a series where we
show you how easy it

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.950
is to deploy solutions from
the Google Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.600
In this episode,
we'll be reviewing

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.110
how to set up a Redis instance
via the Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.260
In case you're unfamiliar, Redis
is an in-memory data structure

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:20.565
store used as a database,
cache, and message broker.

00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:22.815
Let's start by searching for
Redis in the marketplace.

00:00:22.815 --> 00:00:24.767
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.850
You'll see that we have a
few different deployment

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.940
options, from virtual
machines, container images,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.860
to Kubernetes apps.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.230
Each deployment may be deployed
with different operating

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.470
systems, security
patches, or server shapes.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.590
For this demo, we'll choose the
Redis Enterprise Cloud option.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.510
Redis Enterprise Cloud delivers
fully managed Redis enterprise

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.040
as a service.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.710
It offers all the capabilities
of Redis Enterprise

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.710
while taking care of the
operational aspects associated

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.890
with operating Redis in the
most efficient manner on Google

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.630
Cloud Platform.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.460
The landing page will
display information

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:08.040
about the pricing,
documentation, and support.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.560
The pricing information
displays a high-level estimate

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.890
of charges.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.850
Pricing for the solution is
based on hourly consumption

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.640
of Redis Enterprise shards.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.100
Let's click the Subscribe
button to launch the solution.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.770
Start by choosing
a billing account

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.660
and agreeing to the
terms below, which

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.460
are the terms about
subscription fee

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.660
billed monthly and
canceling the service.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.390
You'll also notice
"Pricing Calculator,"

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.790
which can help you see
estimated costs based

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:37.190
on factors like time frame,
shard hours, and data transfer

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:37.690
costs.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.280
We'll choose "Manage
on Provider."

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.000
From, here you create
a Redis subscription.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:58.000
Choose Google Cloud
Platform as your vendor.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.530
Choose a name.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.960
For this video, we'll
choose "test-db."

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.669
Now choose a DB size.

00:02:09.669 --> 00:02:13.415
For this video, I'll choose 1
gigabyte and 25,000 throughputs

00:02:13.415 --> 00:02:13.915
per second.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.590
As you can see, our database
has been created and connected

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.670
to Google Cloud.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.230
Now let's test the database.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.830
We'll run this Python script to
see if the database is working.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.910
Please note, for the
purpose of this demo,

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.420
we use the external DB endpoint.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.730
But we recommend that,
in production, customers

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:41.330
are using internal DB endpoints
within their VPC peering

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:45.620
connection for security
and performance reasons.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.330
There you have it,
a Redis instance

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.090
at the click of a button.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.340
If you enjoyed this video,
please subscribe and hit

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.820
the Like button below.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.240
We encourage you to check
out the GCP Marketplace

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.650
and deploy the
solution on your own.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.630
Thanks for watching.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.680
[MUSIC PLAYING]

